---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { dispensaries } from "../data/dispensaries";

const total = dispensaries.length;
const verified = dispensaries.filter((d) => d.lastVerified).length;
const towns = new Set(dispensaries.map((d) => d.town)).size;
---

<Page
  title="About | VT Dispensary Directory"
  description="How this Vermont cannabis dispensary directory is built, where the data comes from, how often it is verified, and how we make money."
  label="About"
  heading="An independent directory of Vermont's licensed dispensaries"
  intro="No paid placements, no pay-to-rank. Every licensed retailer in the state is listed whether they work with us or not."
>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
    <div class="card p-5"><p class="text-3xl font-black">{total}</p><p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-muted mt-1">Licensed shops</p></div>
    <div class="card p-5"><p class="text-3xl font-black">{towns}</p><p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-muted mt-1">Towns covered</p></div>
    <div class="card p-5"><p class="text-3xl font-black">{verified}</p><p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-muted mt-1">Verified listings</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Where the listings come from</h2>
    <p>
      The spine of this directory is the Vermont Cannabis Control Board's licensee list.
      Every entry carries its CCB retail licence number, which is the only identifier that
      reliably distinguishes two businesses trading under similar names.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contact details, addresses, coordinates, opening hours and amenities are then verified
      against each dispensary's Google Business Profile. That verification pass is dated on
      every listing, so you can see how fresh the information is rather than guessing.
    </p>

    <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    <p>
      We do not publish information we have not verified. Where a dispensary's hours have not
      been confirmed, the listing says so plainly and shows nothing rather than showing a
      plausible guess. The same applies to addresses, phone numbers and amenities.
    </p>
    <p>
      This matters more than it sounds. A directory that invents opening hours sends real
      people to closed doors, and it does it at scale. We would rather show an incomplete
      listing than a confident wrong one.
    </p>

    <h2>How ranking works</h2>
    <p>
      It does not. Listings sort alphabetically or by distance, never by commercial
      relationship. A dispensary cannot buy a higher position, and declining to work with us
      cannot lower one. Where a listing is sponsored, it is labelled sponsored.
    </p>

    <h2>How this is funded</h2>
    <p>
      Outbound links to dispensary websites and menus may be affiliate links, which means we
      may earn a commission when you click through and buy. That never changes what we list
      or how we order it. The full explanation is on the
      <a href="/affiliate/">affiliate disclosure</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If you own or work at a listed dispensary and something here is wrong, tell us and we
      will fix it. Corrections are free and do not require any commercial relationship. The
      same goes for customers who notice a shop has moved, closed or changed hours.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell cannabis, take orders, or handle payments. Nothing here is medical or
      legal advice. Cannabis is legal for adults 21 and over in Vermont and remains illegal
      under federal law, which among other things means you cannot take it across a state
      line.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
